          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Euclid300BC
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclid"}> Euclid
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elements"} Elements
            %li#Tarski
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alfred+Tarski"}> Alfred Tarski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em What is elementary geometry?
                %em The axiomatic method. With special reference to geometry and physics
                Proceedings of an International Symposium held at the Univ. of Calif., Berkeley, Dec. 26, 1957-Jan. 4, 1958 (ed. L. Henkin, P. Suppes, and A. Tarski), Studies in Logic and the Foundations of Mathematics, Amsterdam: North-Holland (1959), pp. 16–29. (
                %a{:href => "http://www.geographicknowledge.de/SeminarLFG/Tarski_Whatiselementarygeometry.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#TG
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alfred+Tarski"} Alfred Tarski
                and Steven Givant,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tarski’s system of geometry
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.27.9012"} web
            %li#MacLane
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Saunders+Mac+Lane"}> Saunders Mac Lane
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Metric postulates for plane geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2309851"} doi:10.2307/2309851
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2309851"} web
          %p Textbook account:
          %ul
            %li#Rees05
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmer+Rees"}> Elmer Rees
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Notes on Geometry
          %p Expository lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Armstrong17
              Drew Armstrong,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Introduction to Geometry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.miami.edu/~armstrong/daVinci/HGnotes.pdf"} pdf
          %p Textbook accounts of the axiomatization of Euclidean geometry include these:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfram+Schwabh%C3%A4user"}> Wolfram Schwabhäuser
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wanda+Szmielew"} Wanda Szmielew
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alfred+Tarski"} Alfred Tarski
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mathematische Methoden in der Geometrie
            %li#Petrunin13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Petrunin"}> Anton Petrunin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Euclidean Plane and its Relatives; a minimalistic introduction
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1302.1630"} arXiv:1302.1630
          %p
            Full formalization of this book in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
            (as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+geometry"} synthetic geometry
            but following Tarski’s work) is discussed at
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel+Braun"}> Gabriel Braun
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Boutry"} Pierre Boutry
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Julien+Narboux"} Julien Narboux
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://geocoq.github.io/GeoCoq/"} GeoCoq
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://gabrielbraun.free.fr/Geometry/Tarski/"} La géométrie de Tarski en Coq
          %p A formalisation of Euclid using diagrammatic reasoning is in
          %ul
            %li
              J. Avigad, E. Dean, J. Mumma,
              %em A formal system for Euclid’s Elements
              ,
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0810.4315v3"} arXiv:0810.4315
              (2009).
          %p
            Another formalization of Euclidean geometry in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Coq"} Coq
          %ul
            %li#Ivashkevich19
              Evgeny V. Ivashkevich,
              %em On Constructive-Deductive Method For Plane Euclidean Geometry
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.05175"}> arXiv:1903.05175
              )
          .footnotes
            %hr/
            %ol
              %li#fn:1
                %p
                  After a famous saying attributed to Hilbert which in some sense heralds the axiomatic spirit: ‘
                  %em> Man muß jederzeit an Stelle von “Punkte, Geraden, Ebenen” “Tische, Stühle, Bierseidel” sagen können
                  ’. The 1891 anecdote is reported by O. Blumenthal in Hilbert,
                  %em Gesammelte Abhandlungen III. Band
                  , Springer Berlin 1935, p.403. The three classes became ‘
                  %em> Liebe, Gesetz, Schornsteinfeger
                  ’ (love, law, chimney-sweep) in Hilbert’s letter to
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gottlob+Frege"} Frege
                  (Dec. 29th 1899). The question raised in Frege’s rejoinder (Jan. 6th 1900) whether his pocket watch is a point is still an open problem.
                  %a{:href => "#fnref:1", :rev => "footnote"} ↩
